      "question": "<h3>A car accelerates uniformly from rest to 20 m/s in 5 s. Its acceleraton is<br />(A) 2 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math><br />(B) 4 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math><br />(C) 5 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math><br />(D) 100 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math></h3>",
      "solution": "<p>a = v / t = 20 / 5 = 4 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math></p>",
      "answer": "A",
