      "question": "<h3>A net force of 10 N acts on a body of mass 2 kg. Its acceleration is<br />(A) 20 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math><br />(B) 5 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math><br />(C) 0.2 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math><br />(D) 12 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math></h3>",
      "solution": "<p>By Newton's second law, a = F / m = 10 / 2 = 5 <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math></p>",
      "answer": "B",
