      "question": "<h3>A wire has a resistance of 2 &Omega;. Its length is doubled and its area of cross-section is halved, keeping the material the same. The new resistance is<br />(A) 2 &Omega;<br />(B) 4 &Omega;<br />(C) 8 &Omega;<br />(D) 1 &Omega;</h3>",
      "solution": "<p>R = &rho; L / A. New R = &rho; (2L) / (A/2) = 4R = 8 &Omega;</p>",
      "answer": "B",
